  "Question": "Which of the following conditions is insufficient to establish that \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is equilateral?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "One interior angle is \\(60^\\circ\\).",
    "B": "All three interior angles are equal.",
    "C": "All three sides are equal.",
    "D": "Two interior angles are \\(60^\\circ\\)."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "If only one angle is \\(60^\\circ\\), the other two angles sum to \\(120^\\circ\\) and are not necessarily equal, so this condition is insufficient.",
